It's not a straw-man as you are still talking about scrolls generated 
randomly. But you don't know which scrolls are generated randomly as 
certain scrolls can be from predetermined source and look like a scroll 
generated randomly. So when you calculate the probability of getting 
?oEW from all srolls in a given game it's way lower than 8%.

And it's still only a probability. You haven't even calculated the 
expectation value and it's variance. So you don't even have any clue if 
the number of ?oEW was within normal variance or way out of the scale.

But what if it was way out of scale? It's still not something to talk 
about, because it's still possible in the confines of the game.

